WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.541
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna stated</b>

2
00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:35.083
<b>that performing sacrifice with true knowledge</b>

3
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:40.250
<b>is far superior to performing it as a mere activity.</b>

4
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.958
<b>Now, a natural question arises:</b>

5
00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:47.000
<b>where can this knowledge be obtained?</b>

6
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.958
<b>Additionally,</b>

7
00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:54.250
<b>Krishna mentioned that the ultimate purpose </b>
<b>of sacrifice is to attain knowledge.</b>

8
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:59.916
<b>So another question emerges: what are </b>
<b>the best sacrifices for acquiring knowledge?</b>

9
00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:04.416
<b>In this verse, Krishna answers</b>
<b>both of these questions:</b>

10
00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:06.541
<b>where to obtain this knowledge</b>

11
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:10.708
<b>and what sacrifices are best for attaining it.</b>

12
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.708
<b>Lord Krishna says that to </b>
<b>acquire spiritual knowledge,</b>

13
00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:22.666
<b>you must approach a wise guru,</b>

14
00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:26.916
<b>humbly ask questions, and serve them,</b>

15
00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:32.250
<b>because only an intelligent person who knows </b>
<b>the truth can impart this knowledge to you.</b>

16
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.208
<b>Only they have known and experienced the truth.</b>

17
00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:39.750
<b>This verse is extremely important</b>

18
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:44.916
<b>because it teaches us about the significance </b>
<b>and glory of gurus in life.</b>

19
00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:51.166
<b>Here, Krishna teaches us that true spiritual </b>
<b>knowledge will not come solely from books,</b>

20
00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:55.958
<b>because real knowledge is that which</b>
<b>arises from life experiences</b>

21
00:01:55.958 --> 00:01:59.708
<b>and brings about change in others' lives as well.</b>

22
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:03.750
<b>For this, we must take shelter of gurus.</b>

23
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.583
<b>Moreover, in this verse, Lord Krishna</b>

24
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:11.791
<b>emphasizes three things: </b>
<b>pranipata, pariprashnena, and seva. </b>

25
00:02:11.791 --> 00:02:14.500
<b>These are the three sacrifices or steps</b>

26
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:20.291
<b>that are essential for a disciple</b>
<b>seeking knowledge to follow.</b>

27
00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:25.291
<b>The first step is pranipata, meaning </b>
<b>humility and surrender.</b>

28
00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:30.625
<b>To receive knowledge from a guru, we </b>
<b>must first relinquish our ego</b>

29
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:34.291
<b>and acknowledge that we lack knowledge,</b>

30
00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:37.250
<b>which is why we seek the guru's guidance.</b>

31
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.125
<b>Here, humility does not merely</b>
<b>mean showing respect,</b>

32
00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:44.125
<b>but complete surrender to the guru.</b>

33
00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:49.916
<b>It means accepting that our spiritual </b>
<b>progress is impossible without the guru.</b>

34
00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:55.125
<b>The renunciation of ego here makes </b>
<b>it akin to a sacrifice.</b>

35
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:56.708
<b>The second step is</b>

36
00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:58.208
<b>pariprashnena,</b>

37
00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:02.541
<b>meaning inquisitiveness and asking </b>
<b>knowledge-enhancing questions.</b>

38
00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:06.208
<b>A good guru will undoubtedly </b>
<b>impart their knowledge,</b>

39
00:03:06.208 --> 00:03:12.250
<b>but if we want to be good disciples and </b>
<b>truly apply this knowledge in our lives,</b>

40
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.375
<b>it is necessary to ask appropriate questions – </b>

41
00:03:15.375 --> 00:03:21.291
<b>questions that help us incorporate </b>
<b>this knowledge into our lives.</b>

42
00:03:21.291 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>However, remember</b>

43
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:29.583
<b>that the purpose of these questions should never </b>
<b>be to doubt or test the guru's knowledge.</b>

44
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:33.958
<b>The sole purpose of these questions is to learn.</b>

45
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:39.666
<b>Here, the complete renunciation of </b>
<b>doubt is also considered a sacrifice.</b>

46
00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:43.708
<b>And finally, the third and last step is seva, service.</b>

47
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:47.583
<b>By serving the guru, a disciple's </b>
<b>mind becomes purified,</b>

48
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:54.625
<b>and this purification of the mind is crucial </b>
<b>for the germination of spiritual knowledge.</b>

49
00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:59.375
<b>The disciple demonstrates their devotion </b>
<b>and surrender through service,</b>

50
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:01.916
<b>thereby obtaining the guru's grace.</b>

51
00:04:01.916 --> 00:04:07.708
<b>And it is through this grace that the </b>
<b>disciple's spiritual progress accelerates.</b>

52
00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:12.833
<b>Service is a symbol of devotion </b>
<b>and gratitude towards the guru.</b>

53
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:18.333
<b>It is also an offering of effort, </b>
<b>making it a sacrifice as well.</b>

54
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:23.416
<b>A disciple without taking these three steps </b>
<b>of humility, inquisitiveness, and service,</b>

55
00:04:23.416 --> 00:04:26.458
<b>will not be able to attain complete knowledge.</b>

56
00:04:26.458 --> 00:04:30.791
<b>Furthermore, in this verse, the guru is </b>
<b>referred to as "tattva-darshi,"</b>

57
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:36.250
<b>Tattva-darshi, meaning one who has </b>
<b>personally experienced true knowledge.</b>

58
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.583
<b>The meaning of guru is not merely a title,</b>

59
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:49.750
<b>but rather, a guru is one who has acquired </b>
<b>knowledge as a disciple and then applied it in life.</b>

60
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.083
<b>Only such a guru can impart </b>
<b>true spiritual knowledge</b>

61
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:58.875
<b>because they have been a disciple themselves</b>
<b>and understand a disciple's mentality.</b>

62
00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:03.333
<b>Moreover, they have sifted through every piece </b>
<b>of knowledge through life experiences</b>

63
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:08.333
<b>and collected only its pure essence for others.</b>

64
00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:12.500
<b>This verse reveals many other important points.</b>

65
00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.875
<b>It also sheds light on the ancient tradition </b>
<b>of the guru-disciple relationship.</b>

66
00:05:17.875 --> 00:05:22.250
<b>It is because of this tradition </b>
<b>that true spiritual knowledge</b>

67
00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:27.333
<b>has been passed down through generations </b>
<b>and is present before us today.</b>

68
00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:31.791
<b>Where a true guru applies</b>
<b>spiritual knowledge in life,</b>

69
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:34.416
<b>refines it through life experiences,</b>

70
00:05:34.416 --> 00:05:40.000
<b>and then distributes the pure and practical </b>
<b>essence of that knowledge among disciples.</b>

71
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.750
<b>And a disciple absorbs this knowledge with </b>
<b>humility, inquisitiveness, and service.</b>

72
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.500
<b>This is the guru-disciple tradition. </b>

73
00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.250
<b>And it began at the very creation of the universe.</b>

74
00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.416
<b>Remember,</b>

75
00:05:53.416 --> 00:05:59.458
<b>Lord Krishna gave the true form of this knowledge </b>
<b>to his disciple, Vivasvan, the Sun God,</b>

76
00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:06.416
<b>and then through the guru-disciple tradition, </b>
<b>this knowledge reached humanity.</b>

77
00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:18.916
<b>Curiosity for knowledge and an attitude of </b>
<b>surrender and service towards gurus</b>

78
00:06:18.916 --> 00:06:25.666
<b>are essential for a disciple</b>
<b>on the path of spirituality,</b>

79
00:06:25.666 --> 00:06:26.791
<b>but</b>

80
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:32.666
<b>they are equally important in </b>
<b>other aspects of life as well.</b>

81
00:06:32.666 --> 00:06:37.875
<b>This lesson is helpful for learning</b>
<b>any new skill in life.</b>

82
00:06:37.875 --> 00:06:39.791
<b>For example,</b>

83
00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:42.083
<b>if you are interested in music</b>

84
00:06:42.083 --> 00:06:46.416
<b>and want to learn to play a new instrument,</b>

85
00:06:46.416 --> 00:06:50.125
<b>you can certainly embark on this path alone.</b>

86
00:06:50.125 --> 00:06:55.125
<b>However, if you seek guidance from a guru,</b>

87
00:06:55.125 --> 00:07:00.583
<b>they can teach you many practical techniques</b>

88
00:07:00.583 --> 00:07:04.958
<b>that can only be learned through experience.</b>

89
00:07:04.958 --> 00:07:13.375
<b>Achieving depth in practice and mastery </b>
<b>in art is difficult without a guru.</b>

90
00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:19.291
<b>A music guru explains every intricacy </b>
<b>of the notes to their disciples,</b>

91
00:07:19.291 --> 00:07:26.666
<b>makes them practice in ways that may </b>
<b>be hard to find in books.</b>

92
00:07:26.666 --> 00:07:30.416
<b>And even if all of this is found in books,</b>

93
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:37.541
<b>no book can understand your mental disposition,</b>

94
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:45.125
<b>which is why a guru's place is </b>
<b>invaluable and incomparable.</b>

95
00:07:45.125 --> 00:07:46.500
<b>Therefore,</b>

96
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:52.916
<b>always learn with an open mind </b>
<b>and respect your gurus.</b>

97
00:07:52.916 --> 00:07:57.750
<b>Apply whatever you learn from them in your life.</b>

98
00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.583
<b>Ask questions, by all means,</b>

99
00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:01.625
<b>but</b>

100
00:08:01.625 --> 00:08:07.833
<b>the purpose of these questions should be </b>
<b>to understand the depth of the subject,</b>

101
00:08:07.833 --> 00:08:12.166
<b>not to test the guru.</b>

102
00:08:12.166 --> 00:08:13.875
<b>Remember,</b>

103
00:08:13.875 --> 00:08:19.208
<b>it is impossible to attain true </b>
<b>knowledge without a guru.</b>

104
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:30.291
<b>In today's social environment, everyone </b>
<b>is connected to everyone else.</b>

105
00:08:30.291 --> 00:08:34.458
<b>You have the opportunity to </b>
<b>learn from numerous people.</b>

106
00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:39.250
<b>Many people are teaching about various subjects.</b>

107
00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.583
<b>But</b>

108
00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:48.583
<b>this also creates a dilemma: what should be </b>
<b>learned and from whom to learn?</b>

109
00:08:48.583 --> 00:08:52.041
<b>In such a situation, understanding yourself</b>

110
00:08:52.041 --> 00:08:57.541
<b>and becoming a good disciple becomes </b>
<b>even more important.</b>

111
00:08:57.541 --> 00:08:59.000
<b>First,</b>

112
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.125
<b>you need to introspect</b>

113
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:07.166
<b>about what genuine improvement </b>
<b>your life truly needs,</b>

114
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:11.791
<b>or what subject you have a genuine interest in.</b>

115
00:09:11.791 --> 00:09:21.333
<b>Are you learning a subject just because it will </b>
<b>make you famous or wealthy without effort?</b>

116
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:25.166
<b>And if someone is showing such a path,</b>

117
00:09:25.166 --> 00:09:26.958
<b>be cautious,</b>

118
00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:33.458
<b>because if someone says that </b>
<b>effort is not necessary at all,</b>

119
00:09:33.458 --> 00:09:36.500
<b>they cannot be a true guru.</b>

120
00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.791
<b>Next, you need to consider</b>

121
00:09:39.791 --> 00:09:47.166
<b>whether you are attracted to a guru </b>
<b>solely because of their popularity.</b>

122
00:09:47.166 --> 00:09:56.875
<b>In today's era, many people lose their way in </b>
<b>the glitz and glamour of popularity and fame.</b>

123
00:09:56.875 --> 00:09:57.916
<b>Yes,</b>

124
00:09:57.916 --> 00:10:02.791
<b>it is possible to gain popularity after hard work,</b>

125
00:10:02.791 --> 00:10:12.041
<b>but to make fame the main goal before even </b>
<b>starting on the path, is completely inappropriate.</b>

126
00:10:12.041 --> 00:10:18.708
<b>If you do this, you may not be able </b>
<b>to become a true disciple.</b>

127
00:10:18.708 --> 00:10:23.666
<b>The goal of a true disciple is to acquire knowledge,</b>

128
00:10:23.666 --> 00:10:31.250
<b>and for this, surrender, a spirit of service, </b>
<b>and humility are essential.</b>

129
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.750
<b>You can choose many paths of progress,</b>

130
00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:35.875
<b>but</b>

131
00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:41.291
<b>never overlook the path of spirituality.</b>

132
00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:48.791
<b>In professional life,</b>

133
00:10:48.791 --> 00:10:55.625
<b>the contribution of a guru or </b>
<b>mentor is incomparable.</b>

134
00:10:55.625 --> 00:11:01.208
<b>It's not just about promotions</b>
<b>or salary increases here.</b>

135
00:11:01.208 --> 00:11:05.250
<b>True professional growth has many aspects,</b>

136
00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:09.708
<b>such as enhancing leadership </b>
<b>abilities within oneself,</b>

137
00:11:09.708 --> 00:11:15.375
<b>focusing on the long-term goals of the </b>
<b>organization while giving up short-term gains,</b>

138
00:11:15.375 --> 00:11:16.958
<b>and yes,</b>

139
00:11:16.958 --> 00:11:22.125
<b>becoming a good mentor for others as well.</b>

140
00:11:22.125 --> 00:11:25.500
<b>And to understand all these aspects,</b>

141
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:31.875
<b>it is extremely important to remain in the</b>
<b>company of capable mentors and gurus.</b>

142
00:11:31.875 --> 00:11:33.625
<b>However,</b>

143
00:11:33.625 --> 00:11:38.458
<b>the situation here is a bit different.</b>

144
00:11:38.458 --> 00:11:43.333
<b>In a professional setting, it is not anyone's </b>
<b>obligation to teach you.</b>

145
00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:53.125
<b>So in such a case, becoming a good disciple </b>
<b>becomes even more necessary.</b>

146
00:11:53.125 --> 00:12:01.291
<b>For this, always keep the three qualities of </b>
<b>humility, respect, and gratitude close to you. </b>

147
00:12:01.291 --> 00:12:07.625
<b>If you are humble, only then will you be able </b>
<b>to recognize the hidden guru in people.</b>

148
00:12:07.625 --> 00:12:13.666
<b>And then, respect for their knowledge and </b>
<b>a sense of gratitude towards them</b>

149
00:12:13.666 --> 00:12:16.708
<b>will inspire them to teach you.</b>

150
00:12:16.708 --> 00:12:19.916
<b>Just have an intense desire to learn;</b>

151
00:12:19.916 --> 00:12:22.708
<b>those who teach will also find you,</b>

152
00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:26.958
<b>and many ways of learning will open up as well.</b>

153
00:12:26.958 --> 00:12:29.208
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

